From 0908015a7befb35ba96b956d132ce7572cc76fd4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VCKing101 <59761021+VCKing101@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 21:22:48 +1030
Subject: [PATCH] Controls: choose each player's controller, or the keyboard

Player 1 was always the keyboard and the first gamepad connected, and
player 2 the next, by the order they arrived. With DS4Windows that gave
the real pad to player 1 and its virtual one to player 2. And a pad
held for player 2 never moved up: DS4Windows connects its new virtual
pad before it removes the old, so a switch of its output left player 1
with no gamepad.

The Controls page now has Player 1 and Player 2 (input.player1,
input.player2; <prefix>_PLAYER1, <prefix>_PLAYER2), or one Controller
row for a profile without GameProfile::second_player: Automatic, the
keyboard and mouse, or a gamepad by its USB vendor and product ids, the
same over USB and Bluetooth. Automatic says what it picked; a chosen
gamepad not connected leaves the player on Automatic and the row says
what it is using. Who gets which pad is worked out in one place
(input/players.*, no SDL, unit-tested), and the renderer opens the pads
it gives each player and closes the rest, on every pad connected or
gone, every change in the menu, and every change of what the port
wants. Each player keeps the pad it has while it can.

The keyboard and mouse buttons go to player 2's pad when chosen, while a
second player is wanted, and the mouse camera of a PortableKit camera
profile stays out of player 1's stick then. A pad held for player 2
moves to player 1, who has none, unless the port says player 2 is in the
game (hle_extension::second_player_playing, interface 8, with
SecondPad::keyboard at the end of the struct).
<prefix>_PLAYER2_PAD_STAYS=1 keeps it player 2's, as before.

Tested with Dissidia 012 on Windows (clang build): scripted runs beside a
DualSense (Automatic, every row cycled, a chosen pad not connected, a
versus battle with player 2 on the keyboard and mouse, a one-player
battle), and the owner cycling Player 1 with a DualSense. The move up
from player 2 with real pads only by the unit tests. Not verified:
DS4Windows, two identical pads, Linux, the Steam Deck, another game.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
